  "behavior": {
    "firmware": "One unique unchanged retained SRAT/optional SLIT from original sealed catalog. Bounded byte decoding of legacy/x2APIC CPU and enabled memory affinity; full sparse32-bit IDs, every qualified CPU mapped. Corrupt/ambiguous/truncated/incomplete/over-bound facts produce complete flat fallback. CPUID geometry and NUMA membership independent.",
    "bounds": {
      "nodes": 32,
      "memory_ranges": 128,
      "enabled_cpu_affinities": 256,
      "srat_records": 1024,
      "slit_localities": 256,
      "table_bytes": 1048576
    },
    "distances": "Optional complete finite directed SLIT only. SRAT same-domain membership remains qualitative without a usable matrix; unknown/unreachable/reserved distances are never exported as measured zero/latency. Internal policy keys are not hardware measurements.",
    "pmm": "Per-node scan cursors/exhaustion hints under original owner. Every local attempt tests real bitmap; fallback retains all free capacity and DMA maximum. Free invalidates hint; no counters/commit/reclaim partitioning. Natural extents stop at a known firmware range boundary; required contiguous global fallback can span nodes.",
    "home": [
      "admitted hard CPU set",
      "actual Running-plus-Ready load",
      "free physical core/SMT",
      "explicit preferred CPU hint",
      "comparable static core class/rank",
      "confirmed resident-stack memory locality",
      "prior/cache locality",
      "stable CPU index"
    ],
    "anchor": "Actual resident top stack page queried before publication only when a NUMA hint can be useful. Unfinished discovery conservatively keeps anchors; a sealed valid SRAT keeps pre-CPU-seal critical anchors, later only confirmed multi-node state needs PTE reads. Missing/invalid/single-node facts skip that owner/query. Exact cache/reserve lifetime retained; no PTE walk in Home, changed stack identity clears hint. No whole-working-set/page-migration claim.",
    "migration": "One donor/eight candidates and one lazy clock retained. Known closer stack may replace first eligible only with not-younger/not-weaker work; otherwise first eligible still transfers under real gap. Exact physical currents, saved RSP/FPU, hard sets, generations and owner barriers remain.",
    "single_node": "One known node or missing SRAT retains original functional allocation/first-eligible behavior. All admitted CPUs and all real free bitmap capacity remain available; no NUMA partition of commit/reclaim."
  },
